            - strong: further decrease the file size
            - text: . The intelligent algorithm ensures that there are no visible differences while more savings are made.
      - term:
        - button "What does TinyPNG do?":
          - heading "What does TinyPNG do?" [level=2]
      - definition:
        - heading "TinyPNG uses smart lossy compression techniques to reduce the file size of your WEBP, AVIF, JPEG and PNG files. By selectively decreasing the number of colors in the image, fewer bytes are required to store the data. The effect is nearly invisible but it makes a very large difference in file size!" [level=3]:
          - paragraph: TinyPNG uses smart lossy compression techniques to reduce the file size of your WEBP, AVIF, JPEG and PNG files. By selectively decreasing the number of colors in the image, fewer bytes are required to store the data. The effect is nearly invisible but it makes a very large difference in file size!
      - term:
        - button "What file formats does TinyPNG support for image compression?":
          - heading "What file formats does TinyPNG support for image compression?" [level=2]
      - definition:
        - heading "Currently, Tinify supports JPEG XL (JXL), AVIF, WebP, JPG, PNG and APNG (animated PNG). We are continuously working to expand our portfolio to include additional formats in the future." [level=3]:
          - paragraph:
            - text: Currently, Tinify supports
            - strong: JPEG XL (JXL)
            - text: ","
            - strong: AVIF, WebP, JPG, PNG
            - text: and
            - strong: APNG
            - text: (animated PNG).
          - paragraph: We are continuously working to expand our portfolio to include additional formats in the future.
      - term:
        - button "Why do I get an optimized JPG when I upload a HEIC image?":
          - heading "Why do I get an optimized JPG when I upload a HEIC image?" [level=2]
      - definition:
        - heading "HEIC is an image format that compresses photos very efficiently, but it is not widely supported by many other devices and platforms. To ensure your images work everywhere, TinyPNG automatically converts HEIC files to JPG, a widely accepted format. If you prefer a next-gen format like AVIF, you can easily convert it with the online optimizer. Avif images offer better quality and smaller file sizes than other formats. The best format you choose depends on how you plan to use the images." [level=3]:
          - paragraph: HEIC is an image format that compresses photos very efficiently, but it is not widely supported by many other devices and platforms. To ensure your images work everywhere, TinyPNG automatically converts HEIC files to JPG, a widely accepted format.
          - paragraph: If you prefer a next-gen format like AVIF, you can easily convert it with the online optimizer. Avif images offer better quality and smaller file sizes than other formats. The best format you choose depends on how you plan to use the images.
      - term:
        - button "Is the privacy of my images ensured?":
          - heading "Is the privacy of my images ensured?" [level=2]
      - definition:
        - heading "At Tinify, your privacy is our top priority. Rest assured, only you have access to the images you upload. We retain them for a maximum of 48 hours, after which they are permanently deleted. For additional details on privacy, please refer to our Terms of Use, specifically sections 8 and 9. These sections provide comprehensive information on privacy policies and data processing operations." [level=3]:
          - paragraph: At Tinify, your privacy is our top priority. Rest assured, only you have access to the images you upload. We retain them for a maximum of 48 hours, after which they are permanently deleted.
          - paragraph:
            - text: For additional details on privacy, please refer to our
            - link "Terms of Use":
              - /url: /terms
            - text: ", specifically sections 8 and 9. These sections provide comprehensive information on privacy policies and data processing operations."
      - term:
        - button "Why did you create TinyPNG?":
          - heading "Why did you create TinyPNG?" [level=2]
      - definition:
        - heading "We frequently use PNG images but were frustrated with the load times. We created TinyPNG in our quest to make our websites faster and more fun to use with the best compression. Since then, we’ve continued to grow. In 2014, we added intelligent compression for JPEG images. In 2016, we introduced support for animated PNG. And today, we also support modern image formats like WebP and AVIF, helping developers and businesses stay ahead with next-generation optimization. Compressing images with the website is free for everyone, and we like to keep it that way! If you like TinyPNG, please contribute by making a donation." [level=3]:
          - paragraph: We frequently use PNG images but were frustrated with the load times. We created TinyPNG in our quest to make our websites faster and more fun to use with the best compression. Since then, we’ve continued to grow. In 2014, we added intelligent compression for JPEG images. In 2016, we introduced support for animated PNG. And today, we also support modern image formats like WebP and AVIF, helping developers and businesses stay ahead with next-generation optimization. Compressing images with the website is free for everyone, and we like to keep it that way! If you like TinyPNG, please contribute by making a donation.
